---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About Carolina Journeys - exploring the trails of the Carolinas">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <header class="mb-12 text-center">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl text-ink font-bold mb-4">About Carolina Journeys</h1>
    </header>
    
    <div class="prose prose-lg mx-auto prose-headings:font-serif prose-headings:text-ink prose-p:text-ink-light">
      <p>
        <strong>Carolina Journeys</strong> began in 2004 as a collection of explorations 
        through the Carolina Piedmont — a tribute to the hidden paths, forgotten roads, 
        and rich history that crisscross our landscape.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        The original articles were written by <a href="/origins">Tom Fowler</a>, who loved 
        to trace the old ways — from the ancient Indian Trading Path to mountain ridges 
        and river fords. His passion for local history, cartography, and the simple joy 
        of following a trail wherever it leads became the foundation of this project.
      </p>
      
      <p>
        Now, his sons continue that journey. Based in Durham, NC, we explore the same 
        landscapes with fresh eyes while honoring the spirit of discovery that started it all. 
        We're hikers, trail runners, history enthusiasts, and amateur cartographers — 
        always curious about what's around the next bend.
      </p>

      <h2>What You'll Find Here</h2>
      
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Trail explorations</strong> — hiking and running through Carolina landscapes</li>
        <li><strong>Local history</strong> — the stories embedded in our geography</li>
        <li><strong>Old roads and paths</strong> — tracing routes that time has nearly forgotten</li>
        <li><strong>Maps and cartography</strong> — because every journey deserves to be mapped</li>
        <li><strong>Urban exploration</strong> — discovering the hidden corners of our cities</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The Name</h2>
      
      <p>
        "Carolina Journeys" captures both the literal travels through the Carolinas and the 
        metaphorical journey of discovery. Some paths are real — you can walk them today. 
        Others exist only in historical records or our imagination. Both are worth exploring.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-12 p-6 bg-parchment-100 rounded-lg border border-trail/20">
        <p class="text-center italic text-ink-lighter mb-0">
          "The journey is the destination."
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
